One piece at a time, the system was assembling someone who knew how to live in this body.

And one piece at a time, I was running out of reasons to insist she wasn't me.

The apartment's ambient light settled back into its violet-rose baseline. The neon veins breathed. The hovering bed hummed. Outside the windows, Eidolon City turned in its endless, glittering orbit   a world I hadn't even entered yet, still trapped in the tutorial, still learning how to exist.

<<system "Module 5: Hygiene and Self-Care." >>

<<system "Beginning in thirty seconds." >>

I sank onto the edge of the bed and pressed my damp palms against my thighs. Thirty seconds. Then the system would teach me how to shower, how to wash, how to maintain this body like the machine it treated me as.

My bladder was empty. My cheeks were burning. My pelvic floor score was ninety-four percent.

And somewhere in the back of my mind, Leo was getting quieter.

[[Familiarization Module 5 Starting|day_4_37_les]]

:: day_4_37_les

The thirty seconds didn't even register. One moment I was sitting on the bed pressing my palms into my thighs, the next the apartment was shifting around me   the violet-rose bleeding into something softer, more domestic. The neon veins in the walls dialed down to a gentle champagne glow, their patterns loosening into slow, lazy whorls that pulsed with the rhythm of calm breathing. The clinical theater of the previous modules retreated. In its place: something that felt almost like a bedroom at dawn. Warm. Quiet. Ordinary.

That was worse, somehow. The clinical modules had been horrifying, but they'd been events   dramatic enough to fight against. This was just... life. Maintenance. The thousand small tasks a body demands when nobody's watching.

<<system "Module 5: Hygiene and Self-Care." >>

<<system "This module covers daily maintenance protocols for the user's avatar, including dermal care, intimate hygiene, hair management, and hormonal skin response." >>

<<leona "Daily maintenance. Like I'm a car.">>

<<system "The comparison is not inaccurate. Complex systems require consistent upkeep to function optimally." >>

The bathroom doorway glowed   a soft invitation. But the system didn't direct me there yet. Instead, the holographic mirror at the vanity activated   just one, angled at waist height   and projected a simple, annotated diagram of a female torso. No nerve maps this time. No blazing orgasm pathways. Just zones marked in color: green for standard care, yellow for caution areas, red for zones requiring specific protocols.

<<system "Beginning with intimate hygiene." >>

<<system "The vaginal canal is a self-cleaning system maintained by a balanced microbiome of lactobacilli bacteria." >>

<<system "Internal pH range: 3.8 to 4.5. Acidic. This acidity prevents pathogenic bacterial and fungal overgrowth." >>

The diagram highlighted the vaginal canal in green   healthy, self-regulating, autonomous. Then red warning markers bloomed around the entrance.

<<system "The following actions disrupt vaginal pH and microbiome balance:" >>

<<system "Internal soaping. Douching. Scented hygiene products. Prolonged submersion in chemically treated water." >>

<<system "Do not insert soap, cleanser, or any surfactant into the vaginal canal. Ever." >>

<<leona "Ever? What if ">>

<<system "Ever." >>

The word hung in the air with a finality that bordered on threat. The system's tone hadn't changed   still flat, still procedural   but the single-word repetition carried weight. This wasn't a suggestion. This was doctrine.

<<system "External washing only. The vulvar surface   outer labia, inner labia, clitoral hood, perineum   should be cleaned daily with warm water. A mild, pH-balanced, fragrance-free cleanser may be used on the outer labia only." >>

<<system "Rinse thoroughly. Residual cleanser causes irritation in sensitive tissue." >>

The diagram demonstrated   a holographic animation showing the correct washing technique. External surfaces only. Gentle. Directional. Front to back, even here   the same cardinal rule from Module 4, applied to every interaction with this part of my body. The animation showed fingers parting the outer labia gently to rinse the folds between   where sweat, discharge, and residual moisture accumulated throughout the day.

<<leona "So every time I shower, I have to... manually...">>

<<system "Correct. The vulvar region contains multiple skin folds that trap moisture, dead cells, and natural secretions. Without regular external cleaning, bacterial overgrowth occurs within 24–48 hours." >>

<<system "The user's avatar has enhanced lubrication response, which increases baseline moisture levels. Daily cleaning is not optional." >>

I absorbed that in silence. Enhanced lubrication. The system had mentioned it during Module 3   my body produced more moisture than standard parameters. Which meant more accumulation. More maintenance. More daily, hands-between-my-legs, careful-with-the-folds upkeep that Leo had never once considered because Leo's anatomy had been external, self-draining, and largely self-sufficient.

<<system "Proceeding to discharge education." >>

A new panel appeared on the mirror   a clinical chart showing a spectrum of colors and textures, each labeled.

<<system "Vaginal discharge is normal and expected. The user will experience daily secretion from the vaginal canal ranging in consistency from thin and clear to thick and white, depending on hormonal cycle position." >>

<<system "Normal discharge: clear to white. Mild scent. No irritation." >>

<<system "Abnormal indicators requiring medical attention:" >>

The chart shifted. Yellow-green patches appeared. Gray. Cottage-cheese texture. Each one labeled with its corresponding infection   bacterial vaginosis, yeast overgrowth, sexually transmitted pathogens. The system listed symptoms beside each: unusual odor, itching, burning during urination, pain during intercourse.

<<leona "I can get infections in there?">>

<<system "The vaginal microbiome exists in a dynamic equilibrium. Disruption   through pH change, immune stress, sexual contact with unscreened partners, or hygiene failure   can result in infection." >>

<<system "The user should monitor discharge daily as a primary health indicator." >>

Monitor discharge daily. Meaning every day   every single day I existed in this body   I'd need to check what came out of me, assess its color, its texture, its smell, and compare it against a clinical chart to determine whether my internal ecosystem was functioning or failing.

Leo had never monitored anything. Leo had showered, toweled off, and moved on with his life in eight minutes.

<<system "Proceeding to skin-fold moisture management." >>

The diagram on the mirror zoomed out   full torso, front view. Yellow zones highlighted beneath the breasts, in the groin creases where thigh met pelvis, and along the inner thighs.

<<system "The user's avatar has pronounced skin-fold regions due to breast size, hip width, and thigh volume." >>

<<system "These areas trap heat and moisture, creating environments conducive to fungal growth and skin maceration." >>

<<leona "Fungal   are you telling me I can get mold under my boobs?">>

<<system "Cutaneous candidiasis and intertrigo are common in skin-fold regions with inadequate ventilation. The inframammary fold is a primary risk zone for the user's breast configuration." >>

The diagram highlighted the crescent-shaped zone beneath each breast   the fold where heavy tissue met the ribcage, pressed together by gravity, warm and dark and persistently damp. I looked down at my own chest. At the real, physical fold I could see if I lifted slightly. A hidden pocket of skin-on-skin that Leo had never possessed and Leona would carry everywhere.

<<system "After bathing, the user must dry all skin-fold regions thoroughly. Patting, not rubbing. Ensure no residual moisture remains in the inframammary fold, groin creases, or inner thigh junction." >>

<<system "In high-humidity environments or after physical exertion, antifungal powder may be applied to these zones prophylactically." >>

I filed that information in a mental drawer I hadn't known I needed. Antifungal powder. Under my breasts. As a preventive measure. Because the body the system had given me was, among its many features, a humidity trap.

<<system "Proceeding to undergarment protocol." >>

The wardrobe in the main room hummed   audible even from here. The system projected a fabric comparison chart on the mirror: four swatches rendered in holographic texture.

<<system "Cotton: breathable, moisture-wicking, recommended for daily wear. Allows adequate airflow to vulvar region." >>

<<system "Silk: low breathability, high friction reduction. Suitable for limited duration." >>

<<system "Synthetic mesh: poor moisture management. Traps heat. Increases infection risk with prolonged wear." >>

<<system "No underwear: maximum ventilation. Recommended during sleep cycles to allow tissue recovery." >>

<<leona "You're recommending I sleep without ">>

<<system "Extended vulvar ventilation during rest periods reduces cumulative moisture exposure by approximately 30% and lowers candidal infection probability." >>

<<system "The user's enhanced lubrication output makes this recommendation particularly relevant." >>

There it was again. Enhanced lubrication output. The system wielded the phrase like a diagnostic code, stripping the reality   my body's enthusiastic, uncontrollable wetness   of everything human and filing it under maintenance requirements. I was a machine that leaked, and the system was teaching me to manage the leak.

<<system "Proceeding to hair care." >>

The champagne-toned lighting in the apartment warmed a degree. The wardrobe's secondary compartment opened, and a hairbrush slid forward on the automated rail   not the sleek chrome of the other fixtures, but something almost organic. A paddle brush with flexible bristles, its handle curved to fit a hand smaller than Leo's had been.

<<system "The user's avatar has hair extending to the waist. Approximately 72 centimeters from crown to terminal length." >>

<<system "Hair of this length requires daily detangling to prevent matting, split propagation, and structural damage." >>

A holographic model appeared beside the vanity   a featureless feminine figure with hair identical to mine in length and texture. The system animated a demonstration: starting at the ends, working upward in short, gentle strokes, never dragging through tangles from root to tip.

<<system "Begin at the distal ends. Short strokes. Work progressively toward the scalp." >>

<<system "Forcing the brush through tangles from root to tip causes breakage, split ends, and pain." >>

The brush hovered in front of me. I took it. The handle was warm   body-temperature, like everything else in this apartment   and fit my palm with a precision that suggested it had been sized specifically for Leona's grip.

I reached behind my head and gathered a section of hair. It came forward over my shoulder in a thick, silky cascade   honey-brown with golden streaks that caught the warm light like threads of actual metal. The hair was beautiful. Objectively, undeniably beautiful. It was also tangled from every module I'd been dragged through   knots forming where I'd tossed my head, where I'd bent forward, where I'd buried my face in my arms on the bed.

I started at the ends. Short strokes. The bristles caught immediately   a small tangle, nothing dramatic   and I worked through it with gentle, repetitive passes. The holographic model demonstrated the same motion in parallel. I matched it. Stroke. Stroke. Stroke. The tangle gave way, and the freed strands slipped through the bristles like water.

<<system "Correct technique. Proceed upward." >>

I worked higher. More tangles. More patience. The brush moved through my hair in small, rhythmic increments   a meditative, surprisingly soothing process that silenced the screaming in my head for the first time since the transformation. Just... brushing. The soft pull at my scalp. The whisper of bristles through silk. The slow accumulation of smooth, detangled waves falling over my shoulder and down across my bare breast in a sheet of warm gold.

Ten minutes passed before I realized I'd finished one side and started the other without being told.

<<system "Hair care technique: proficient." >>

<<system "Daily detangling time estimate for the user's hair volume: 10–15 minutes." >>

<<leona "Fifteen minutes. Every day. Just for hair.">>

<<system "Additionally: the user should condition hair after washing to maintain keratin integrity. Wet hair is structurally weaker and must not be brushed aggressively. Air-drying is preferable to heat-drying for long-term health." >>

<<system "Sleeping with hair braided or loosely tied reduces tangling by approximately 60%." >>

Braiding my hair before bed. Conditioning after washing. Never brushing when wet. Leo had used a two-in-one shampoo-body wash and spent forty-five seconds on his hair   total, start to finish, including rinsing.

<<system "Proceeding to hormonal skin response." >>

The mirror's display shifted to a dermal analysis   a close-up render of skin surface at magnified scale. Pores, sebaceous glands, collagen fiber patterns.

<<system "The user's avatar operates on a full estrogen-progesterone hormonal cycle. Skin response varies by cycle phase." >>

<<system "Follicular phase, days 1–13: estrogen rising. Skin clarity increases. Sebum production decreases. Complexion at optimal luminosity." >>

<<system "Ovulation, day 14: estrogen peak. Maximum skin clarity. Enhanced facial vasodilation produces visible 'glow' effect." >>

<<system "Luteal phase, days 15–28: progesterone rising. Sebum production increases. Pore congestion likely. Hormonal acne may present along the jawline, chin, and forehead." >>

<<leona "I can get acne now? From my own hormones?">>

<<system "Progesterone stimulates sebaceous glands. The resulting increase in skin oil, combined with the cellular turnover rate of the luteal phase, creates conditions for comedonal and inflammatory acne." >>

<<system "Preventive protocol: gentle non-comedogenic cleanser twice daily during luteal phase. No harsh exfoliants. No pore-stripping products   these trigger rebound oil production." >>

The mirror displayed a two-week skincare calendar   different products, different frequencies, different techniques depending on where in the hormonal cycle the user currently sat. A routine that shifted and adapted every fourteen days. A routine that required tracking. Planning. Understanding where in a cycle she was, what her skin was about to do, and preempting it with the correct intervention at the correct time.

Leo had washed his face with whatever bar soap was in the shower.

<<system "Additional note: hormonal fluctuations affect hair texture, body odor profile, and sweat composition across the cycle." >>

<<system "The user may notice changes in hair oiliness, underarm scent, and skin sensitivity that vary from week to week. These are not malfunctions. They are features of the hormonal architecture." >>

Features. Not bugs.

<<system "Module 5 complete." >>

The champagne lighting held. The brush rested in my hand   warm, familiar now, bristles threaded with a few strands of honey-brown that caught the glow. My hair hung in smooth, detangled waves over both shoulders, spilling across my breasts, reaching nearly to my waist. It smelled faintly of something I couldn't identify   not perfume, not product, just... me. Whatever Leona smelled like beneath the panic and the sweat and the chrome. Clean. Warm. Alive.

I set the brush on the vanity. Looked at the girl in the single bathroom mirror. She looked tired. Not Module 3 tired   not the wide-eyed, trembling, violated exhaustion of forced genital contact. A quieter tired. The tiredness of someone who'd just been shown the maintenance manual for a machine she hadn't ordered and was beginning to understand she couldn't return.

This body wasn't a costume. It wasn't a glitch to be patched. It was a system   complex, demanding, self-regulating in some ways and utterly dependent on her care in others. It had a pH to maintain and discharge to monitor and skin folds to dry and hair to brush and hormones that would change her face every two weeks and underwear that mattered and a way to pee that required tissue and direction and attention.

Leo had existed in his body like a tenant who never read the lease. Leona didn't have that luxury. This body came with terms and conditions, and every single one required her participation.

The apartment settled. The neon veins breathed. Outside the windows, Eidolon City's skyline had shifted from the deep violets of artificial dusk to the amber haze of approaching artificial dawn   hours passing in the simulation while I'd been trapped in tutorials. The light caught the tangled chrome of distant hover-lanes and painted long golden streaks across my bare shoulders.

<<system "Module 6: Menstrual Cycle Simulation." >>

<<system "Beginning in sixty seconds." >>

I set the brush down gently. Pulled my hair over one shoulder   a gesture I hadn't learned from any module, a gesture that just happened, automatic and natural and terrifying in its casualness. I walked back to the bed. Sat on its edge. Thighs together. Hands in my lap. Spine curved in the posture that already felt more native than Leo's slouch.

Sixty seconds until the system taught me how to bleed.

I pressed my smooth, freshly brushed hair against my cheek and breathed in the scent of a girl I was running out of energy to deny.

